From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xun2202 <98207886+Xun2202@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:00:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(browse): restore full title and shared secondary filter
 row

Address user feedback that plugin names are too small, popular/latest should sit on a second row matching library categories, and natural return to the top leaves a hidden header and empty spacer. Shared fix with Mihon 0093. Remove the compact source title/filter combination and restore normal AppBarTitle typography and available width. Keep filters on a persistent horizontally scrollable second row in regular/search/selection states, preserving saved searches and all actions. Share 40dp compact/48dp regular secondary-row metrics with library category rows and global search; draw Anikku category divider within the row instead of adding height. The source panorama uses bare PanoramaMasonry while the library uses its fast-scroll wrapper. Move boundary observation into the masonry viewport and remove the outer duplicate, so both variants follow the leading content spacer and commit revealed navigation after inertia reaches the start. Preserve the original fling kernel and gesture policy. Update the title/row-height regression for compact and tall windows and add real raw/fast panorama pointer-release tests, recording positive release offset/velocity and checking inertial arrival, header/content alignment and stable departure from the start.
---
